This case tests careful analysis. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {6, 8, 12, 15, 18, 21, 25, 30, 33, 34};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 30) return steps; if (a[mid] < 30) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

Work through the problem below. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {-3, 1, 0, -3, 5, 2, 7, 4, -4};
int acc = a[0];
for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > acc) acc = a[i];
return acc;

Consider the instance described. What does this string routine return?
String s = "iudxi";
StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();
for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) out.append(s.charAt(i));
return out.toString();

This problem calls for a trace. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {1, 4, 5, 8, 12, 15};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 23) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 23) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

A question from the practice set: What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(30);
Node b = new Node(20);
Node c = new Node(25);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Read carefully and compute the result. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {7, 8, 9, 13, 14, 17, 18, 19, 20, 22, 23};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 20) return mid; if (a[mid] < 20) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return -1;

Solve the problem that follows. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {1, 8, -3, 9, 5, -1, 9, 1, -1};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) acc += a[i];
return acc;

Check the reasoning in this case. What does this string routine return?
String s = "bbaaaabb";
int i = 0, j = s.length() - 1;
while (i < j) { if (s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)) return false; i++; j--; }
return true;

